{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false},"description":"Scans one local file for well-known cryptographic/hashing constant tables authored from public specifications: AES S-box, inverse S-box, Te0/Td0, Rcon; MD5 T-table and init; SHA-1/256/512 init and round constants (K prefix-anchored); CRC-32 reflected table and polynomials 0x04C11DB7/0xEDB88320; DES S-boxes; Blowfish P-array; ChaCha/Salsa20 \"expand 32/16-byte k\"; TEA/XTEA/XXTEA deltas; FNV/MurmurHash3/xxHash primes; DEFLATE base tables; standard and URL-safe Base64 alphabets plus a custom-alphabet heuristic; and P-256/secp256k1/Curve25519 parameters. Returns findings[] {algorithm, kind (sbox|iv|round_constant|table|magic|curve_param), evidence_kind=inferred, file_offset, resolved section, byte_order le|be|any, length}, a finding_coverage block, an algorithm_summary, and the file subject. Each match is observed bytes; algorithm attribution is inferred and shared constants may be reported under several algorithms. It does NOT prove the algorithm is reachable or used, does NOT extract key material or plaintext, and does NOT decrypt or unpack. It reads the file once (up to 256 MiB) without executing the target, without network access and without writing files; findings are bounded (256 per constant, 4096 total) with truncation signalled in finding_coverage. Non-executable input gives a \"file\" subject with null sections; every caveat is listed in limitations.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"examples":[{"path":"/artifacts/application"},{"path":"/artifacts/sample.bin"}],"properties":{"path":{"description":"Absolute filesystem path to the selected local file","minLength":1,"pattern":"^[^\\x00]*$","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"name":"identify_crypto_constants","outputSchema":{"$defs":{"__schema0":{"pattern":"^ev_[a-f0-9]{64}$","type":"string"},"__schema1":{"